How many rows does the LEFT JOIN return?

```sql
CREATE TABLE author (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT);
CREATE TABLE book (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, author_id INTEGER, title TEXT);
INSERT INTO author VALUES (1, 'Wisława'), (2, 'Naguib'), (3, 'Isabel');
INSERT INTO book VALUES (10, 1, 'a'), (11, 1, 'b'), (12, 2, 'c'), (13, NULL, 'd');
SELECT count(*) FROM author AS a LEFT JOIN book AS b ON b.author_id = a.id;
```

An order has three lines worth 10, 15 and 5, and was sent in two shipments. What does this query print?

```sql
CREATE TABLE ord (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, customer TEXT);
CREATE TABLE line (order_id INTEGER, amount INTEGER);
CREATE TABLE shipment (order_id INTEGER, carrier TEXT);
INSERT INTO ord VALUES (1, 'Rania');
INSERT INTO line VALUES (1, 10), (1, 15), (1, 5);
INSERT INTO shipment VALUES (1, 'post'), (1, 'courier');
SELECT sum(l.amount)
FROM ord AS o
JOIN line AS l ON l.order_id = o.id
JOIN shipment AS s ON s.order_id = o.id;
```

A self join lists the matches of a round-robin tournament. How many rows does it count?

```sql
CREATE TABLE team (name TEXT);
INSERT INTO team VALUES ('Ajax'), ('Boca'), ('Celtic'), ('Dynamo');
SELECT count(*) FROM team AS a JOIN team AS b ON a.name < b.name;
```
